# Fundraising emails & PDF (canonical)

**Source of truth:** `lib/fundraising/pdfAttachmentPolicy.ts` → `fundraisingDocNeedsPdfAttachment(type)`.

## Matrix

| Type | Trigger | Email body | PDF |
|------|---------|------------|-----|
| **D1** | Public apply | Full HTML acknowledgement | No |
| **D2–D4** | Welcome pack / access link | Full HTML | No |
| **D5–D8, D12** | Lifecycle / Documents Send | Full HTML | No |
| **D6** | Lookup share / Documents if sent | Full HTML | No |
| **D9** | Mark Paid / Documents Send | Short cover | **Yes** (client visual) |
| **D10** | Mark Paid / Documents Send | Short cover | **Yes** (client visual) |
| **D11** | RCTI lifecycle / Documents (if enabled) | Short cover | **Yes** |
| **D13** | Termination pack / Documents | Short cover | **Yes** |
| **D14–D15** | Internal download | Usually no partner email | No |
| **D16** | Lookup bank save | Full HTML security confirm | No |
| **D17** | Lookup bank save → admin | Full HTML admin alert | No |
| **OTP** | Lookup login | Short code mail | No |

## Patterns

**With PDF (invoice-style):** short cover (`buildFundraisingDocCoverPlainText` / `CoverHtml`) + PDF attachment. Do not paste full D9/D10 HTML into the email body.

**Without PDF:** send full `htmlBody` / apply HTML as before. Do not invent empty PDF attachments.

## Code paths

| Path | Behaviour |
|------|-----------|
| Documents Send | `needsPdf` → preview/iframe client PDF + cover; else HTML only |
| Mark Paid | Always D9+D10 client PDFs + settlement cover |
| `issueFundraisingDocuments` | PDF only if allow-listed; else full HTML |
| Apply D1 / D16 | HTML only |
| API lifecycle resend | Same allow-list |

## Client PDF quality (D9/D10)

`lib/fundraising/htmlToPdfClient.ts`: always render full HTML via iframe `srcdoc`, capture full scroll height (explicit html2canvas height/width), multi-page jsPDF.  
**Never** capture the Documents preview panel (`max-h-[70vh] overflow-auto`) — that crops Payment Destination / footer.  
Reject blank/white canvases before send; Resend via `emailService.sendResponse({ attachments: File[] })`.


## Do not

- Attach PDF to D1 / welcome / D16 “for consistency”
- Put full settlement HTML in the email when a PDF is attached
- Expand the allow-list without product confirmation
